Planex hover_drag_interaction — boundary-CLOSING demo (v0.6 prototype)
======================================================================
Validates: hover+drag+cancel+tap with px_interaction + affordances.
Counterpart of hover_drag_4abs.c (ADR-0006 evidence → ADR-0016).

[1] hover sweep (40 mouse moves)...
    status after sweep: hover: item Elderberry
    estimate writes during sweep: 0
    observer fires during sweep:  0 (old demo: ~80)

[2] drag slot 1 to slot 4 (60 samples)...
    committed: slot1=4 slot4=1 (reordered)
    hook fired 2 times for 62 events (old demo: 0 hooks,
    3 Estimates × 62 writes instead)

[3] drag slot 0 toward slot 3, then ESC (cancel)...
    cancelled (reason="esc pressed"), slot0=0 (unchanged)

[4] quick tap on slot 2 (2 samples, 6px)...
    displacement: 6px → classified as TAP (<4px would be
    noise); velocity 0.20 px/ms

[5] gesture derivation from trajectory measures...
    swipe: displacement=540 path=540 velocity=7.5 px/ms
    → derivable (old demo verdict: "Gesture: NOT POSSIBLE")

Final state:
  mouse moves fed:    130
  estimate writes:    2 (exactly 2 — one reorder commit)
  observer fires:     0 (order[0] never changed: 0; +2 init)
  item order:         Apple Elderberry Cherry Date Banana 
  afford_at(slot 3):  found (drag process)

=== Boundary-closing demo complete ===

HACK RETIREMENT (vs hover_drag_4abs.c):
  HACK 1 (mouse as Estimate, 60fps churn):   RETIRED — samples are inert
  HACK 2 (hover as Estimate):                RETIRED — pure region query
  HACK 3 (drag state as 3 Estimates):        RETIRED — one process object
  HACK 4 (begin-drag as REQUEST):            RETIRED — begin is a phase
  HACK 5 (mouse move as EXPRESS intent):     RETIRED — sample ≠ act
  HACK 6 (hover read per frame):             KEPT (by design — perception
                                             reads the stream as input)
  HACK 7 (poll for mouse-up):                N/A headless; real backends
                                             deliver PX_EV_MOUSE_UP/WHEEL

Verdict for ADR-0016:
  - The 5 of 7 hacks that forced PROCESS into STATE are gone.
  - The estimate-write count for the whole session is 2 (one
    reorder), versus ~O(events) in the old demo.
  - Cancel is a first-class outcome; gesture is derivable.
  - Prototype status: evidence, not promotion. The 5 canonical
    abstractions are untouched.
